The 'utils-global' folder contains shared utility functions and types that are used across multiple packages within the project, promoting code reuse and consistency. It's structured as a separate TypeScript package with its own configuration files including package.json, tsconfig.json, and tsconfig.tsbuildinfo to manage compilation and build processes independently. This folder serves as a centralized location for common functionality that doesn't belong in any specific domain package but is essential for the overall project's operation.
